{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"876646958482198528","content":"Sentinel Stuffy\nWondrous item (requires attunement)\n\nA plush toy that more often than not finds the new owner, before the owner finds it. This doll attunes itself to you upon being picked up. While attuned to it and on your person, you gain a +1 to your AC and all saving throws. The stuffy acts as an Unseen Servant with the following changes, it has an AC of 13, 10 hit points, and a Strength of 10.The Sentinel Stuffy also has minimal sentience with an Intelligence of 4(-3), Wisdom of 10(+0), and a Charisma of 16(+3) It cannot speak, but understands all languages spoken by its owner. If you are separated from the Sentinel Stuffy for over 24hrs you will lose attunement, during this time the Stuffy will do all it can to get back to you.If you were to die due to overwhelming damage or from failing death saves, the Sentinel Stuffy takes your place when dying, becoming inanimate, and ending your attunement.\n\nOdd Heart\nWondrous item (requires attunement)\n\nThis item is one that has always been with you, your own heart, and its potential only unlocked by an experimental surgery. If you manage to survive the surgery you will awaken to your heart being encapsulated in a containment chamber of your own choosing and connected by a tubing or a cord to your chest. After the surgery you will find yourself permanently under the effect of Sanctuary(DC15) until you are unattuned. Whenever you roll a hit die you always take maximum healing. Once attuned to the Odd Heart you cannot unattune to it unless you die or undergo a more dangerous reversal surgery.\n\nSymbiotic Nature.\nThe heart can't be removed from you while you're attuned to it, and you can't voluntarily end your attunement to it. If you're targeted by a spell that ends a curse or enter an anti-magic zone, your attunement to the heart ends, and you immediately fall unconscious and start making death saves.\n\nPhlogiston Pidgin\nWondrous item (requires attunement) \n\nThis prosthetic tongue was made with magi who have had their tongues forcibly removed. Taking a lump of molten phlogiston and molding it carefully, a person could replace their lost tongue. \n\nThe extra dimensional energies inherent in the Phlogiston imbue the attuned with the languages of all the planes. While attuned you can cast Tongues on yourself a number of times equal to half your proficiency bonus rounded down and resets on a long rest. You can also cast Speak with Animals, Plants, and Dead at will. \n\nYou also gain proficiency in one of the following abilities: Deception, Intimidation, or Persuasion. If you are already proficient in the chosen ability you gain expertise instead. \n\nOwl Feather Arrows\nAmmunition \n\nFletched with feathers gifted by the Owl Folk of the Fae Wild, these arrows fly silently through the air avoiding nearly all detection. You can add your Wisdom modifier to your attack bonus when firing these arrows or bolts.\n\nWhen you fire one of these arrows or bolts from hiding, regardless if it hits, the intended target needs to make a perception check vs. your initial stealth check to detect you. If it misses the target makes the check with disadvantage and normally if it hits. If you are not detected you do not need to use the hide action again.\n\nWhen a rogue uses these arrows or bolts they get an extra 1d6 of Sneak Attack damage.\n\nSea Farer's Foil (unique)\ncommon, wondrous\nrapier\n\nThe blade is mounted on a hilt made of sea stone and carved to look like the body of a swordfish. Rumor has it that the piece of stone used was actually a piece of a Lodestone. \n\nWhile wielding this rapier and fighting underwater, you cannot receive disadvantage on attack rolls due to not having a swim speed.","created_at":"2021-08-16T05:21:49.714000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"876697237697228850","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"876646958482198528","content":"Punisher’s Cloak\nwondrous item, varies (requires attunement)\n\nThis cloak seems to be made from the wings of some foul beast. Through mystical or medical means the cloak is attached to the skin of whoever attunes to it. The abilities granted by the cloak vary depending on rarity. This cloak has 5 charges that recharge on a long rest. The rare versions of the wings are not as well adapted to the user, but still have sparks of life within them and can sometimes be forced to shield yourself or your allies. As a reaction to you or a friendly creature (within 5ft) being targeted by a melee, ranged, or spell attack or forced to make a Dexterity saving throw, you can spend a number of charges to grant half, three-quarter, or total cover. 1 charge, 3 charges, or 5 charges, respectively. \n\nThe very rare version, additionally, gives you +1 to AC and a flight speed of 50ft.","created_at":"2021-08-16T05:22:31.268000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"876697411987320842","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
